          %p
            In the category of modules over some commutative ring, the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-th
            divided power of a module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is equivalently descibed as the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔖
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A^{\otimes n})^{\mathfrak{S}_{n}}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
            under the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔖
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{S}_{n}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\otimes n}
            by permutation of the factors. Note that the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-th
            symmetric power
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{n}(A)
            of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in a symmetric monoidal category is described as the coequalizer of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n!
            permutations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\otimes n} \rightarrow A^{\otimes n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔖
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A^{\otimes n})_{\mathfrak{S}_{n}}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinvariants"} coinvariants
            by the action of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔖
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{S}_{n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_{n}(A^{*}))^{*} = \Gamma_{n}(A)
            which probably means that these powers can be interpreted as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+modalities"} graded exponential modalities
            in a kind of graded
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+linear+logic"} differential linear logic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+0"} characteristic 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi n
